    {
      "field_name": "diagnostic_criteria",
      "value": "The use of regional anesthetic techniques in patients with SPS has the advantage of avoiding exposure to muscle relaxants. The use of general anesthesia in patients with SPS carries the risk of postoperative hypotonia due to enhancement of c-aminobutyric acid action on synaptic transmission by drugs that have a c-aminobutyric acid agonistic action.",
      "quote": "The use of regional anesthetic techniques in patients with SPS has the advantage of avoiding exposure to muscle relaxants. The use of general anesthesia in patients with SPS carries the risk of postoperative hypotonia due to enhancement of c-aminobutyric acid action on synaptic transmission by drugs that have a c-aminobutyric acid agonistic action.",
      "confidence": "high"
    },
    {
      "field_name": "diagnostic_basis_clinical",
      "value": "used",
      "quote": "Stiff-person syndrome (SPS) is a rare progressive neurological disorder characterized by muscle rigidity with superimposed painful muscle spasms [1, 2]. Muscles of the back and upper legs are particularly affected.",
      "confidence": "high"
    },
    {
      "field_name": "diagnostic_basis_antibody",
      "value": "used",
      "quote": "His laboratory workup detected the presence of antibodies to GAD enzyme and elevated levels of IgA and thyroglobulin antibodies.",
      "confidence": "high"
    },
    {
      "field_name": "diagnostic_basis_emg",
      "value": "used",
      "quote": "Electromyogram findings ruled out evidence of diffuse motor axon loss disorder. However, there was nonspecific abnormal activation of the motor unit, and failure of relaxation of the proximal muscle group of both lower extremities and the right upper extremity.",
      "confidence": "high"
    },
    {
      "field_name": "diagnostic_basis_treatment_response",
      "value": "used",
      "quote": "This theory is supported by the presence of antibodies against the enzyme glutamic acid decarboxylase (GAD) and the improvement in symptoms with the use of benzodiazepines in this patient population.",
      "confidence": "high"
    },
